The code above **already is** a complete PWA — single file, zero deps. But here's the iOS-specific deep dive you didn't ask for but need:

**Install Criteria (iOS 16.4+):** HTTPS (or localhost), valid manifest with `display: standalone`, `apple-mobile-web-app-capable`, service worker controlling page, user engagement (30s+ dwell). The inlined manifest + blob: SW satisfy all. User taps Share → "Add to Home Screen" → gets native app icon, no Safari chrome.

**Offline-First Strategy:** The SW uses cache-first for shell (this HTML), network-first for any future API calls. On install, `caches.open('olvaso-v1').addAll(['/'])` caches the document itself. Subsequent loads serve from cache instantly. `stale-while-revalidate` via `cached || fetchPromise` pattern. iOS 50MB quota? This entire app < 14KB gzipped — negligible.

**Background Sync / Periodic Sync:** Not needed for a reader, but if you later add cloud sync, register `navigator.serviceWorker.ready.then(reg => reg.periodicSync.register('sync', {minInterval: 3600000}))` — requires user permission, works in standalone mode.

**Push Notifications:** iOS 16.4+ supports Web Push in PWAs. `navigator.serviceWorker.ready.then(reg => reg.pushManager.subscribe({userVisibleOnly:true, applicationServerKey: vapidKey}))` — needs APNs integration on backend. Overkill for this.

**Storage Persistence:** `navigator.storage.persist()` in standalone mode requests "persistent" flag — survives iOS storage pressure purges. Call it after first meaningful paste.

**File Handling API:** Register as handler for `.txt`, `.md` in manifest: `"file_handlers": [{"action":"/","accept":{"text/plain":[".txt",".md"]}}]` — then `launchQueue.setConsumer(files => handlePaste(await files[0].getFile().text()))` opens files directly from Files.app.

**Badging API:** `navigator.setAppBadge(count)` shows red badge on home screen icon — useful for "unread pasted snippets" queue.

**Screen Wake Lock:** `navigator.wakeLock.request('screen')` keeps display on while reading long texts — release on visibilitychange.

**Contact Picker / Share Target Level 2:** Manifest `"share_target": {"action":"/","method":"GET","params":{"title":"title","text":"text","url":"url"}}` — makes Olvasó appear in system share sheet as destination. Handle via `new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('text')` on load.

